to a world to find out where a schedule spends its time. Every schedule","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that runs on the world then records each system’s runs in it:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","world.resources.insert(SystemProfile())","world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 0, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","frame.run(on: &world)","","let timings = world.resources[SystemProfile.self].timings","print(timings.map(\\.name))","\/\/ Prints \"[\"Gravity\", \"Movement\"]\"","print(timings.map(\\.runs))","\/\/ Prints \"[2, 2]\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" also holds the total, average, longest and latest time of the system’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"runs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A run’s time covers the system’s own work, measured on a continuous clock: not its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conditions, nor the commands it queued, which apply after its wave. A system its conditions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"skip doesn’t run, so nothing is recorded for it. Systems in the same wave run at the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"time, so their times can add up to more than the wave took. Insert a new profile to start","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SchedulingSystems":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedulingsystems","abstract":[